  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "s01",
      "program": "sgiemu",
      "family": "behaviour",
      "target": {
        "function": "fp_check_result"
      },
      "question": "In target.exe, find the function that emits, in the translator from MIPS code to x86-64 code, the check that sends a translated floating-point operation back to the interpreter when its result is not a normal number (a NaN, an infinity or a denormal), letting zero through. Give the address where that function starts."
    },
    {
      "id": "s02",
      "program": "sgiemu",
      "family": "chain",
      "target": {
        "function": "exec",
        "callee": "regimm"
      },
      "question": "In target.exe, one function executes the MIPS instructions that branch on the sign of a register (with or without link, likely or not) or trap when a register compares with an immediate value. Exactly one other function calls it directly. Give the address where that calling function starts."
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "program": "c5xtools",
      "family": "behaviour",
      "target": {
        "function": "first_tok"
      },
      "question": "In target.exe, find the function that returns the first token of a source line (the directive or mnemonic), skipping a label that starts in the first column, and where the rest of the line starts. Give the address where that function starts."
    },
    {
      "id": "s04",
      "program": "c5xtools",
      "family": "chain",
      "target": {
        "function": "field_at",
        "callee": "dma_operand"
      },
      "question": "In target.exe, one function arms, after an operand that uses direct memory addressing has been evaluated, the relocation for its data-page-relative address when it refers to exactly one symbol, and clears it otherwise. Exactly one other function calls it directly. Give the address where that calling function starts."
    },
    {
      "id": "s05",
      "program": "moppe-emu",
      "family": "behaviour",
      "target": {
        "function": "sio_read_ctrl"
      },
      "question": "In target.exe, find the function that returns the value of the status register selected by the register pointer of one channel of the serial communications controller, and resets the pointer. Give the address where that function starts."
    },
    {
      "id": "s06",
      "program": "moppe-emu",
      "family": "chain",
      "target": {
        "function": "serial_tick",
        "callee": "sio_tick"
      },
      "question": "In target.exe, one function advances the transmitters of the two channels of the serial communications controller to a given time: it finishes a byte being shifted out, moves the next buffered byte into the shifter and raises the transmit interrupt. Exactly one other function calls it directly. Give the address where that calling function starts."
    },
    {
      "id": "s07",
      "program": "flint",
      "family": "behaviour",
      "target": {
        "function": "parse_variable"
      },
      "question": "In target.exe, find the function that parses the name in a variable declaration, declares the variable, and returns the index of the name in the constant table for a global variable (0 for a local one). Give the address where that function starts."
    },
    {
      "id": "s08",
      "program": "flint",
      "family": "chain",
      "target": {
        "function": "compile_and_maybe_run",
        "callee": "fl_stats_walk"
      },
      "question": "In target.exe, one function walks a compiled function and, recursively, the functions among its constants, adding up functions, bytecode bytes and constants for a statistics report. Exactly one other function calls it directly. Give the address where that calling function starts."
    }
